    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Owen Reilly present this bright and spacious, dual-aspect two-bedroom apartment ideally located in the heart of Grand Canal Dock. Positioned on the forth floor with a south facing aspect towards the city centre overlooking Pearse Street, the property is presented in excellent condition and benefits from superb natural light, a designated parking space. In addition new windows have been recently installed.\r\n\r\nThe well proportioned accommodation comprises entrance hall with generous storage and a hot press, a bathroom, a bright open-plan living/dining room with access to a south-facing balcony overlooking Pearse Street, a fully fitted kitchen, and two spacious double bedrooms. The principal bedroom benefits from an en suite bathroom and direct access to a private balcony overlooking the internal courtyard. The dual-aspect layout providing excellent natural light throughout the day, with morning sun to the rear and evening sun to the front.\r\n\r\nThis well-maintained apartment offers comfortable city living in one of Dublin’s most sought-after locations. Viewing is highly recommended!\r\n\r\nMore about this location...\r\n\r\nGrand Canal Dock is a vibrant urban quarter with a variety of neighbourhood bars, bistros, cafes and restaurants clustered around the historic city dock. The iconic Grand Canal Theatre and the Marker Hotel face onto the scenic, Martha Schwartz designed waterfront plaza. The DART and LUAS are within ten minutes walking distance, while St Stephen’s Green, Ballsbridge and the IFSC are all within 20 minutes’ walking distance. The locality benefits from a wide range of multinational employers including Google, Accenture, Salesforce and State Street."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hallway (4.53m x 1.47m) MAX\r\nSpacious L-shaped entrance hall with timber flooring, storage, hot press and intercom.\r\n\r\nLiving/dining room (5.23m x 4.67m)\r\nBright dual-aspect reception room with access to the south-facing balcony. Newly installed windows.\r\n\r\nKitchen (3.54m x 1.97m)\r\nModern fully fitted kitchen with integrated appliances to include oven, hob, microwave, extractor fan, dishwasher, fridge/freezer and washer/dryer.\r\n\r\nMain bedroom (4.39m x 3.54m)\r\nSpacious double bedroom with timber flooring, built in wardrobes, views of the internal courtyard and access to the private balcony and en-suite.\r\n\r\nEn-suite (1.76m x 1.45m)\r\nPart-tiled bathroom with shower cubicle, WC, WHB and mirrored cabinet.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (3.54m x 3.14m)\r\nGenerous double bedroom with fitted wardrobes and views of the internal courtyard.\r\n\r\nBathroom (2.36m x 1.92m)\r\nPart-tiled bathroom with bath/shower unit, WC, WHB and mirrored cabinet."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Prime location in the heart of Grand Canal Dock.\r\nSouth facing.\r\nSpacious dual-aspect two-bedroom apartment.\r\nNew windows.\r\nTwo balconies.\r\nPresented in excellent decorative condition throughout.\r\nLocated on the third floor with lift access.\r\nDesignated parking space.\r\nBright and spacious open-plan living/dining area.\r\nExcellent storage including a hot press and hallway storage.\r\nWell-maintained development with landscaped communal gardens.\r\nWithin walking distance of Grafton Street, Bord Gáis Energy Theatre, cafés, restaurants, shops and transport links."
      },
      {
